<title>FRANCE: Roussel-Uclaf net 9-mth net up 13.4 pct.</title>
<headline>Roussel-Uclaf net 9-mth net up 13.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to Sept, 30 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net income excl exceptionals	   1,185  vs	   1,045</p>
<p>    Net income				   2,175  vs	   1,044</p>
<p>    Cashflow				     1,454  vs	   1,421</p>
<p>    Turnover				    12,938  vs	  11,966</p>
<p>NOTE - Roussel-Uclaf said sales rose on a comparable basis, restating the 1995 figures to reflect changes in the group structure, by 5.1 percent in the period. It said net income on a like-for-like basis rose 13.4 percent. Roussel also said it &quot;remains confident in its ability to achieve its targets for 1996.&quot; It gave no figures. Roussel is 56.51 percent held by Hoechst.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
